            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We separate the integrand into the sum of two fractions so that we can simplify each term. So, we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b(3 + 2x)/(x)dx|= \u222b((3)/(x) + (2x)/(x))dx; = \u222b((3)/(x) + 2)dx; = 3\u222b(1)/(x)dx + 2\u222bdx; = 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + C.]</span></p><p>Lastly, let&#x27;s rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C,]</span> we can always write <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C =3 \\ln K]</span> where <span class=\"math\">[MATH: K]</span> is some other constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3\\ln|x|]</span> term, and we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b(3 + 2x)/(x)dx|= 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + C; = 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + 3\\ln K; = 3\\ln (K|x|) + 2x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We separate the integrand into the sum of two fractions so that we can simplify each term. So, we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b(3 + 2x)/(x)dx|= \u222b((3)/(x) + (2x)/(x))dx; = \u222b((3)/(x) + 2)dx; = 3\u222b(1)/(x)dx + 2\u222bdx; = 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + C.]\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant [MATH: C,] we can always write [MATH: C =3 \\ln K] where [MATH: K] is some other constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with [MATH: 3\\ln|x|] term, and we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b(3 + 2x)/(x)dx|= 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + C; = 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + 3\\ln K; = 3\\ln (K|x|) + 2x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
