    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nRecall that for [MATH: x >0,] we have\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(\\ln{x}) = \\dfrac 1 x.]\n\nContent:\nWe can generalize this to all values [MATH: x\\neq 0] by including an absolute value inside the natural logarithm:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(\\ln{|x|}) = \\dfrac 1 x.]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, the integral of the reciprocal function is\n[MATH: \\int \\dfrac 1 x \\,\\textrm{d}x = \\ln |x| + C.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Integrating a Reciprocal Function\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac 2 x\\right)\\, \\textrm{d} x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient [MATH: 2] out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of [MATH: \\dfrac 1 x,] and get\n[MATH: \u222b((2)/(x))dx|= 2\u222b(1)/(x)dx; = 2\\ln|x|+ C.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \u222b(7)/(x)dx.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 7\\ln|x|+ C]\nb. [MATH: 7 + \\ln|x|+ C]\nc. [MATH: (7)/(\\ln|x|) + C]\nd. [MATH: \\ln|x|+ C]\ne. [MATH: (\\ln|x|)/(7) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \u222b(dx)/(9x).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (1)/(9)\\ln|x|+ C]\nb. [MATH: \\ln (9 \u2212 x) + C]\nc. [MATH: \\ln (9 + x) + C]\nd. [MATH: \\ln|x|+ 9x + C]\ne. [MATH: 9\\ln|x|+ C]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the integral of [MATH: \\dfrac 1 {2x} + 3x] with respect to [MATH: x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nApplying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n[MATH: \u222b((1)/(2x) + 3x)dx|= \u222b(1)/(2x)dx + \u222b3xdx; = (1)/(2)\u222b(1)/(x)dx + 3\u222bxdx; = (1)/(2)\\ln|x|+ 3 \u22c5 (x^{1 + 1})/(1 + 1) + C; = (\\ln|x|)/(2) + (3x^{2})/(2) + C.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nFind the integral of [MATH: (2)/(x) \u2212 (1)/(sqrt(x))] with respect to [MATH: x.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: x \u2212 2x^{1/2} + C]\nb. [MATH: 2\\ln|x|\u2212 (2)/(x) + C]\nc. [MATH: \\ln|x|+ 2x^{1/2} + C]\nd. [MATH: 2\\ln|x|\u2212 2x^{1/2} + C]\ne. [MATH: \\ln|x|\u2212 x^{1/2} + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nFind the integral of [MATH: (3)/(5x) + 3x] with respect to [MATH: x.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (7)/(5)\\ln|x|+ (5x^{2})/(2) + C]\nb. [MATH: (3)/(5)\\ln x + (5x^{2})/(2) + C]\nc. [MATH: \\ln x + (7x^{2})/(2) + C]\nd. [MATH: (5)/(3)\\ln|x|+ (x^{2})/(2) + C]\ne. [MATH: (3)/(5)\\ln|x|+ (3x^{2})/(2) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Tutorial: Simplifying the Arbitrary Constant Using the Laws of Logarithms\n\nContent:\nFor any constant [MATH: C,] we can always write [MATH: C = \\ln K,] where [MATH: K>0] is some other constant. Then, using the laws of logarithms, we can write\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u222b(1)/(x)dx|= \\ln|x|+ C; = \\ln|x|+ \\ln K; = \\ln (K|x|).]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Integrating a Reciprocal Function and Simplifying the Arbitrary Constant Using the Laws of Logarithms\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is the antiderivative of [MATH: \\dfrac {3+2x} {x} ?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe separate the integrand into the sum of two fractions so that we can simplify each term. So, we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b(3 + 2x)/(x)dx|= \u222b((3)/(x) + (2x)/(x))dx; = \u222b((3)/(x) + 2)dx; = 3\u222b(1)/(x)dx + 2\u222bdx; = 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + C.]\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant [MATH: C,] we can always write [MATH: C =3 \\ln K] where [MATH: K] is some other constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with [MATH: 3\\ln|x|] term, and we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b(3 + 2x)/(x)dx|= 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + C; = 3\\ln|x|+ 2x + 3\\ln K; = 3\\ln (K|x|) + 2x.]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nWhat is the antiderivative of [MATH: (6 + 7x)/(x)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 6\\ln (K|x|+ 7)]\nb. [MATH: 6\\ln (K|x|) \u2212 7x]\nc. [MATH: 6\\ln (K|x|) + 7x]\nd. [MATH: \\ln (K(6 + 7|x|))]\ne. [MATH: \\ln (7K|x|+ 6)]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nWhat is the antiderivative of [MATH: (8)/(3x)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (8)/(3)\\ln (K|x|)]\nb. [MATH: (1)/(3)\\ln (8K|x|)]\nc. [MATH: (1)/(3)\\ln (8|x|+ K)]\nd. [MATH: \\ln ((8)/(3)K|x|)]\ne. [MATH: (8)/(3)\\ln (|x|+ K)]"
  }
